# Phishing Website Detection Using Deep Learning

This project is a **Deep Learning-based Phishing Website Detection System** that predicts whether a website URL is **Phishing** or **Legitimate**.

## 🧠 Deep Learning Models Used

The project uses a combination of:

* **CNN (Convolutional Neural Network)** – used to learn important patterns from the URL features.
* **LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory)** – used to learn sequential patterns and relationships in the input data.

These models are used together for phishing URL classification.

The models are implemented using **TensorFlow and Keras**.

## 📊 Dataset

The model is trained using a **phishing website dataset** containing examples of both **phishing and legitimate URLs**.

The dataset contains URL-based features that are used for training and classification.

> The dataset is not included in this repository because of its large file size.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

* Python
* TensorFlow
* Keras
* CNN
* LSTM
* NumPy
* Pandas
* Scikit-learn
* HTML
* CSS
* JavaScript
* Google Colab

## 🔍 How It Works

```text
Website URL
     ↓
Feature Extraction
     ↓
Data Preprocessing
     ↓
CNN + LSTM Model
     ↓
Prediction
     ↓
Phishing / Legitimate
```

## 🎯 Objective

The objective of this project is to use **Deep Learning and Cybersecurity techniques** to detect potentially phishing websites from their URLs.


